 "text": "So what does this add to Claude Code by hand? Planning becomes contracts on a board. Parallel work gets a worktree per task. Review gets an independent verifier, merging gets a gate, and mistakes become checks. The Mac's load and limits are watched, and memory lives in git. And you're asked only what's yours to decide. Underneath, it's the same Claude Code. Its permission rules, hooks and status line are how VibeSwitcher works.",
